it9175 bundles two things that are not original work:

1. `it9175/firmware.bin` — the IT9175 firmware image, extracted from the vendor Android application. It is vendor firmware, not covered by this
   project's MIT licence. It is kept for private interoperability testing only;
   do not redistribute it. The protocol code works without it (the driver
   simply cannot start a blank dongle).

2. `vendor/usb/` (pyusb, BSD-3-Clause) and
   `vendor/windows/x64/libusb-1.0.dll` (libusb, LGPL-2.1). Their licences are
   in `vendor/usb/LICENSE` and `vendor/windows/x64/LICENSE`.

## Upstream

The Java core (`it9175/java`) is a port of OpenDTV's `It9175Tuner` / `AfaCmd` /
`It9175Data` (`jpdcs/OpenDTV`, MIT). The register tables in `it9175/tables.py`
were generated from that same source. The Python driver, `docs/protocol.md` and
the verification record are original to this project.

The direction is written down on purpose: **OpenDTV is the original; this tree
references it.** On 2026-11-03 the 295-command parity log was run against
OpenDTV's own `It9175Tuner` with identical canned inputs — byte-identical writes,
so the two cores agree on init and two tunes.

## Provenance marker

`it9175-pbcnx` is a visible provenance/attribution string in the Python and Java
metadata (`--version`, `It9175Device.PROVENANCE`). It is intended to make the
origin searchable and to encourage the MIT notice to travel with copies. It is
**not** telemetry: it performs no network or device I/O, carries no user or
device identifier, and changes no protocol bytes.
